          decompressed data. A malicious server (when using the default                                   
          `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient`/`AsyncHTTPClient`/`HTTPClient` to fetch responses) or a malicious client
          (when the `HTTPServer` is started with `decompress_request=True`) can supply a small, highly    
          compressed payload that expands into effectively unlimited memory, causing a denial of service  
